<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The mod's own sound effects.

  ⚠ EVERYTHING HERE MUST BE ORIGINAL OR PROPERLY LICENSED. Ripped game audio - Skyrim's above
  all - is copyrighted and may not be redistributed, exactly as this project already rules for
  another mod's ART ("their art is a ruler, never a source"). The repo is PUBLIC, so committing
  such a file is distribution before the mod is published anywhere, and git history keeps it
  after a later delete. All three clips were made by the user - the two breaths on 2026-08-06,
  the landing recorded the same day and wired up on 2026-08-12.

  clipPath is relative to the mod's Sounds/ folder and carries NO extension. RimWorld accepts
  .wav, .mp3, .ogg, .xm, .it, .mod and .s3m (read off ModContentLoader.AcceptableExtensionsAudio,
  not assumed) - so these .mp3 files need no conversion.
-->
<Defs>

  <!--
    A DRAGON'S FIRE BREATH.

    context MapOnly + a distRange, so it is heard from where the breath actually is and fades
    with distance. NOT onCamera: this project's notebook records that a sound authored
    onCamera must be played with PlayOneShotOnCamera, and played positionally is inaudible from
    anywhere but its own tile. These are positional, and Thing_DragonBreath plays them that way.

    maxSimultaneous 2 - a dragon can only breathe one at a time, but two dragons might, and a
    breath restarting on top of itself is what turns a roar into a wall of noise.
  -->
  <SoundDef>
    <defName>Dovahkiin_DragonBreathFire</defName>
    <context>MapOnly</context>
    <maxSimultaneous>2</maxSimultaneous>
    <subSounds>
      <li>
        <grains>
          <li Class="AudioGrain_Clip">
            <clipPath>DragonBreathFire</clipPath>
          </li>
        </grains>
        <volumeRange>32~38</volumeRange>
        <!-- A little pitch variation so repeated breaths in one fight do not read as a
             copy-paste. Narrow on purpose: wide pitch ranges make a roar sound comical. -->
        <pitchRange>0.94~1.06</pitchRange>
        <distRange>0~45</distRange>
      </li>
    </subSounds>
  </SoundDef>

  <SoundDef>
    <defName>Dovahkiin_DragonBreathFrost</defName>
    <context>MapOnly</context>
    <maxSimultaneous>2</maxSimultaneous>
    <subSounds>
      <li>
        <grains>
          <li Class="AudioGrain_Clip">
            <clipPath>DragonBreathFrost</clipPath>
          </li>
        </grains>
        <volumeRange>32~38</volumeRange>
        <pitchRange>0.94~1.06</pitchRange>
        <distRange>0~45</distRange>
      </li>
    </subSounds>
  </SoundDef>

  <!--
    A DOVAH COMING DOWN. Played by Comp_AlduinFlight.DoLandingImpact, at the cell he actually
    lands on - AFTER the pounce has moved him, or a dive would be heard where he took off from.

    The clip was recorded 2026-08-06 and sat in Sounds/ unused until 2026-08-12: it postdates the
    last edit to this file by twelve hours and simply never got a def. **A media file in the
    folder is not a wired-up asset** - nothing warns about one nobody references, because from
    RimWorld's point of view there is nothing to warn about.

    distRange runs further than the breaths (0~60 against 0~45): an impact heavy enough to stun
    everything within 2.4 cells should carry past the fight it happens in, and unlike a breath it
    is one short event rather than a sustained roar, so it does not crowd the mix.

    maxSimultaneous 1 - one dragon landing twice inside a second is the dive re-firing, not two
    impacts, and layering the clip on itself turns a thud into a flam.
  -->
  <SoundDef>
    <defName>Dovahkiin_DragonLanding</defName>
    <context>MapOnly</context>
    <maxSimultaneous>1</maxSimultaneous>
    <subSounds>
      <li>
        <grains>
          <li Class="AudioGrain_Clip">
            <clipPath>DragonLanding</clipPath>
          </li>
        </grains>
        <volumeRange>34~40</volumeRange>
        <pitchRange>0.94~1.06</pitchRange>
        <distRange>0~60</distRange>
      </li>
    </subSounds>
  </SoundDef>

  <!--
    TAKE-OFF. Grounded -> Flight or Grounded -> Soar, played by Comp_AlduinFlight.EnterState,
    gated on the SOURCE state exactly as the landing is - so Soar <-> Flight is silent, because
    he never leaves the ground for it.

    2.237s, and he is standing still when it fires, so unlike the circling loop below there is no
    drift problem and a plain positional one-shot is right.

    ⚠ .wav, where everything else here is .mp3. Both are in
    ModContentLoader.AcceptableExtensionsAudio (.wav .mp3 .ogg .xm .it .mod .s3m), and clipPath
    carries NO extension either way, so nothing needs converting.
  -->
  <SoundDef>
    <defName>Dovahkiin_DragonTakeOff</defName>
    <context>MapOnly</context>
    <maxSimultaneous>1</maxSimultaneous>
    <subSounds>
      <li>
        <grains>
          <li Class="AudioGrain_Clip">
            <clipPath>DragonTakeOff</clipPath>
          </li>
        </grains>
        <volumeRange>34~40</volumeRange>
        <pitchRange>0.96~1.04</pitchRange>
        <distRange>0~60</distRange>
      </li>
    </subSounds>
  </SoundDef>

  <!--
    CIRCLING, TAKE 1 AND TAKE 2. The dragon ALTERNATES them - a saved flag in Comp_AlduinFlight,
    not a random roll: the two takes are the same length and similar in character, so a coin flip
    would routinely play one three legs running and read as a single looping clip, which is the
    very thing having two of them is meant to avoid.

    ⚠ TWO SEPARATE DEFS, NOT TWO GRAINS IN ONE. A single def with both clips as grains would let
    RimWorld pick, and RimWorld picks at RANDOM - which is precisely what we are avoiding. The
    alternation has to live where it can be remembered across a save.

    ⚠ EACH RUNS 15.192s, AND A PlayOneShot IS PINNED TO A FIXED WORLD POSITION FOR ITS WHOLE
    LENGTH. It is therefore anchored at the CENTRE of the circle rather than at the dragon, who at
    3.42x would otherwise fly a long way from his own noise. That is sound because circling is
    bounded - he stays within roughly one dragonCirclingRadius of the centre. Anything that needs
    audio to FOLLOW him across the map wants a Sustainer maintained per tick, not this.

    distRange is wider than the breaths: this is the sound of something enormous overhead, and it
    should reach a player whose camera is on the colony rather than on the dragon.
  -->
  <SoundDef>
    <defName>Dovahkiin_DragonFlightCircling1</defName>
    <context>MapOnly</context>
    <maxSimultaneous>1</maxSimultaneous>
    <subSounds>
      <li>
        <grains>
          <li Class="AudioGrain_Clip">
            <clipPath>DragonFlightCircling1</clipPath>
          </li>
        </grains>
        <volumeRange>30~36</volumeRange>
        <!-- Narrower than the one-shots on purpose: pitch-shifting a 15-second bed is audible as
             a wobble, where on a 2-second thud it just reads as variation. -->
        <pitchRange>0.98~1.02</pitchRange>
        <distRange>0~70</distRange>
      </li>
    </subSounds>
  </SoundDef>

  <SoundDef>
    <defName>Dovahkiin_DragonFlightCircling2</defName>
    <context>MapOnly</context>
    <maxSimultaneous>1</maxSimultaneous>
    <subSounds>
      <li>
        <grains>
          <li Class="AudioGrain_Clip">
            <clipPath>DragonFlightCircling2</clipPath>
          </li>
        </grains>
        <volumeRange>30~36</volumeRange>
        <pitchRange>0.98~1.02</pitchRange>
        <distRange>0~70</distRange>
      </li>
    </subSounds>
  </SoundDef>

</Defs>
